The rule: on log and reserve ops only, delete calories or protein unless that number appears in the person's own words, within max(10, 5%). The words are this message plus the previous user message, so the answer to the one clarifying question counts. Numbers are read as digits ("1,200", "1.2k", "900kcal") or as words ("twelve hundred", "a thousand"). The rule runs before the transcript push so that the engine, the next model call and the training log all see the cleaned op (route.ts logRun appends the transcript to data/edit-log-v2.jsonl). A working prototype is at <the session scratchpad>/analysis/log-calories/figures.ts. Only calories and protein need handling: the log and reserve schemas (primitives.ts:764-765) strip any other key.

